{"type":"message","id":"f4114ddd","parentId":"989b014e","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:40:47.157Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_h4e8t2oxwzv9_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Normalize state value to standard string\n  normalizeState(dbState, repetitions) {\n    // Handle undefined, null, or empty states\n    if (!dbState || dbState === '') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle numeric states (convert to string)\n    const stateStr = String(dbState).trim();\n    \n    // Handle \"2.0\" or \"2\" which means Review\n    if (stateStr === '2.0' || stateStr === '2') {\n      return 'review';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"1.0\" or \"1\" which means Learning  \n    if (stateStr === '1.0' || stateStr === '1') {\n      return 'learning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"3.0\" or \"3\" which means Relearning\n    if (stateStr === '3.0' || stateStr === '3') {\n      return 'relearning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"0\" or \"0.0\" which means New\n    if (stateStr === '0' || stateStr === '0.0') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle string states\n    const validStates = ['new', 'learning', 'review', 'relearning'];\n    if (validStates.includes(stateStr.toLowerCase())) {\n      return stateStr.toLowerCase();\n    }\n    \n    // Default: if repetitions is 0, treat as new\n    if (!repetitions || repetitions === 0) {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Otherwise treat as review\n    return 'review';\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Set initial values with defaults\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    card.difficulty = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    \n    // Normalize state before mapping\n    const normalizedState = this.normalizeState(dbCard.state, dbCard.repetitions);\n    \n    // Map normalized state to FSRS State\n    switch (normalizedState) {\n      case 'new':\n        card.state = State.New;\n        card.due = now; // New cards are due immediately\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'learning':\n        card.state = State.Learning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'relearning':\n        card.state = State.Relearning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'review':\n      default:\n        card.state = State.Review;\n        // For review cards, set due date properly\n        if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n        } else {\n          card.due = now;\n        }\n        \n        // Calculate stability from interval for review cards\n        // FSRS stability roughly correlates to interval * ease_factor\n        // This is an approximation - the actual stability is learned through reviews\n        const interval = dbCard.interval || 0;\n        const easeFactor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n        card.stability = Math.max(0.1, interval * easeFactor); // Minimum stability of 0.1\n        \n        // Calculate elapsed_days from last_review or due_date\n        if (dbCard.last_review) {\n          card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.last_review) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          // If no last_review but has due_date, calculate from due_date\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.due) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else {\n          card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        }\n        break;\n    }\n    \n    // Set last_review if available\n    if (dbCard.last_review) {\n      card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n    } else {\n      card.last_review = now;\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: rating = Rating.Easy; break; // Perfect maps to Easy with bonus\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result - pass card first, then now\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days from now to the scheduled due date\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    const intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling.card.lapses,\n      state: stateMap[scheduling.card.state] || 'new',\n      stability: scheduling.card.stability,\n      difficulty: scheduling.card.difficulty\n    };\n  },\n  \n  // Calculate preview intervals without modifying card\n  previewIntervals(card, ratingValue) {\n    const fsrsCard = this.dbToCard(card);\n    return this.repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue);\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = FSRSEngine;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772160047153}}
{"type":"message","id":"4a6303aa","parentId":"f4114ddd","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:41:05.711Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the issue better. Let me trace through the code:\n\n1. The `previewIntervals` function in `fsrs.js` calls `dbToCard(card)` to convert the database card to an FSRS Card object, then calls `repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue)`.\n\n2. Looking at the `repeat` function:\n   - It maps rating 1-5 to FSRS ratings\n   - But there's a problem: rating 5 (Perfect) maps to `Rating.Easy`, which is the same as rating 4 (Easy)\n   - Also, it only handles ratings 1-4 in the switch statement\n\n3. In `server.js`, the preview endpoint loops from 1 to 5:\n   ```javascript\n   for (let rating = 1; rating <= 5; rating++) {\n     const result = FSRSEngine.previewIntervals(card, rating);\n     if (result) {\n       previews[rating] = formatInterval(result.interval);\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. Looking at the FSRS engine, rating 5 should ideally give a bonus interval, but it's being mapped to Rating.Easy just like rating 4.\n\nWait, let me check the actual issue more carefully. Let me also check if there are sample cards in the database to test with.\n\nActually, looking at the code more carefully:\n\nIn `fsrs.js`:\n- Rating 1 (Again) -> Rating.Again\n- Rating 2 (Hard) -> Rating.Hard  \n- Rating 3 (Good) -> Rating.Good\n- Rating 4 (Easy) -> Rating.Easy\n- Rating 5 (Perfect) -> Rating.Easy (same as Easy!)\n\nThis is one issue - rating 5 (Perfect) should give a bonus beyond Easy.\n\nBut there's another issue I see: in `repeat()` function, it calculates interval like this:\n```javascript\nconst dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n\n\nconst intervalMs = dueDate - now;\nconst intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n```\n\nThis calculates the interval from NOW to the due date. But that's not quite right - it should calculate from the review time to the due date. Also, for preview purposes, we might want to see the interval for the NEXT review, not the interval from now.\n\nLet me check what the actual issue is. I should run the server and see what's happening. First let me check if there's any test or demo data available.","thinkingSignature":"1a508adc8ab5f6f17fe4e2039d6df1b10eecfc074c535f4e361ab572ec54a203"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me check the database and also verify how the server is running:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_mo7795wkga2b_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/data/"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":14916,"output":580,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23285,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160047157}}
