{"type":"message","id":"f1a7247e","parentId":"8f017c2f","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:41:37.289Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the stability is calculated as 6 * 2.5 = 15, which is incorrect. The FSRS algorithm has its own stability that's learned through reviews. The problem is that we're calculating stability incorrectly.\n\nAlso, I notice that the elapsed_days is about 0.63 days (about 15 hours), which is correct since the last review was on 2026-02-26 and today is 2026-02-27.\n\nNow let me check how the FSRS library actually expects stability to be handled. Looking at the fsrs.js library usage, the issue might be:\n\n1. We're calculating stability incorrectly (interval * ease_factor is wrong)\n2. We should initialize stability to a default value for review cards instead\n\nLet me also check the actual intervals that would be applied when we review vs what's shown in the preview.\n\nLet me test what happens when we actually process a review:","thinkingSignature":"f4cc138ee787fc03d973a6cde1c232d0d6029b353325a6f323c35e637aa4f4d1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_s8xr6zym0x3a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst FSRSEngine = require('./src/fsrs');\n\nconst db = new Database('./data/cards.db');\nconst card = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = 1').get();\n\n// Convert to FSRS card\nconst fsrsCard = FSRSEngine.dbToCard(card);\n\n// Test actual review\nconsole.log('Testing actual review:');\nfor (let rating = 1; rating <= 5; rating++) {\n  // Create a fresh card for each test\n  const testCard = FSRSEngine.dbToCard(card);\n  const result = FSRSEngine.repeat(testCard, rating);\n  console.log('Rating', rating, ':', result ? 'interval=' + result.interval + ' days, state=' + result.state : 'null');\n}\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":1768