{"type":"message","id":"04021194","parentId":"6b906fc3","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:41:57.540Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the difference between:\n- Backend API returns: [0 days, 15 days, 17 days, 19 days, 19 days]\n- Frontend fallback returns: ['1m', '7m', '6d', '20d', '23d']\n\nThe backend returns much larger intervals. Let me also compare what the preview API returns with the formatInterval:","thinkingSignature":"3a5ca4e5afea46f9624f0ccb16474ce3c875c8fcef27f4383375a82408ceb8d3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7oe3x378n058_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst FSRSEngine = require('./src/fsrs');\n\nfunction formatInterval(days) {\n  if (days < 1) {\n    return Math.round(days * 24) + 'm';\n  } else if (days < 30) {\n    return Math.round(days) + 'd';\n  } else if (days < 365) {\n    return Math.round(days / 30) + 'mo';\n  } else {\n    return Math.round(days / 365) + 'y';\n  }\n}\n\nconst db = new Database('./data/cards.db');\nconst card = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE id = 1').get();\n\nconsole.log('Backend preview API (formatted):');\nfor (let rating = 1; rating <= 5; rating++) {\n  const result = FSRSEngine.previewIntervals(card, rating);\n  console.log('Rating', rating, ':', result ? formatInterval(result.interval) : 'null');\n}\n\nconsole.log('\\\\nFrontend fallback:');\n// Frontend calculateIntervals function\nfunction calculateIntervals(card) {\n  let { interval, ease_factor, repetitions } = card;\n  ease_factor = ease_factor || 2.5;\n  interval = interval || 0;\n  \n  return [\n    '1m',  // Again\n    Math.max(1, Math.round(interval * 1.2)) + 'm',  // Hard\n    repetitions === 0 ? '1d' : (repetitions === 1 ? '6d' : Math.round(interval * ease_factor) + 'd'),  // Good\n    repetitions === 0 ? '4d' : Math.round(interval * ease_factor * 1.3) + 'd',  // Easy\n    repetitions === 0 ? '10d' : Math.round(interval * ease_factor * 1.5) + 'd'  // Perfect\n  ];\n}\nconsole.log(calculateIntervals(card));\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":18727,"output":539,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27055,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160106776}}
{"type":"message","id":"88c21883","parentId":"04021194","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:41:57.592Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_7oe3x378n058_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Backend preview API (formatted):\nRating 1 : 0m\nRating 2 : 15d\nRating 3 : 17d\nRating 4 : 19d\nRating 5 : 19d\n\nFrontend fallback:\n[ '1m', '7m', '6d', '20d', '23d' ]"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":36,"aggregated":"Backend preview API (formatted):\nRating 1 : 0m\nRating 2 : 15d\nRating 3 : 17d\nRating 4 : 19d\nRating 5 : 19d\n\nFrontend fallback:\n[ '1m', '7m', '6d', '20d', '23d' ]","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772160117589}}
{"type":"message","id":"bd699217","parentId":"88c21883","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:42:05.067Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issues clearly:1. **Backend issues:**   - Rating 1 (Again) shows 0m instead of something like \"10m\" (learning step)   - Rating 5 (Perfect) shows 19d, same as Rating 4 (Easy) - should be higher   - The intervals are much higher than they should be due to incorrect stability calculation2. **Root cause:**   - The stability is calculated incorrectly as `interval * ease_factor`   - Rating 5 (Perfect) is mapped to the same FSRS rating as Rating 4 (Easy)Now I understand the problems. Let me fix them:1. Fix the stability calculation - use a more appropriate initial stability2. Fix Rating 5 (Perfect) to give a bonus interval3. Maybe also check if the rating mapping is correctLet me look at what changes need to be made:","thinkingSignature":"95c28dfc7a2493eeabcbf9681399912bf2974b0af47202781bca45096cd6541f"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the issues. Let me analyze them:\n\n**Problems found:**\n\n1. **Rating 5 (Perfect)** shows the same interval as Rating 4 (Easy) - because both map to `Rating.Easy` in the FSRS engine\n2. **Rating 1 (Again)** shows 0m - this goes to relearning state but the preview should show a learning interval\n3. **Stability calculation is wrong** - currently `interval * ease_factor` which gives unrealistic values (15 for a card with 6 day interval)\n4. **Intervals are inflated** due to incorrect stability\n\nLet me fix the FSRS engine:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_vm5qgzunmcai_1","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/src/fsrs.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":19353,"output":357,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27499,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160117592}}
{"type":"message","id":"ea0dcb8f","parentId":"bd699217","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:42:05.086Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_vm5qgzunmcai_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Normalize state value to standard string\n  normalizeState(dbState, repetitions) {\n    // Handle undefined, null, or empty states\n    if (!dbState || dbState === '') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle numeric states (convert to string)\n    const stateStr = String(dbState).trim();\n    \n    // Handle \"2.0\" or \"2\" which means Review\n    if (stateStr === '2.0' || stateStr === '2') {\n      return 'review';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"1.0\" or \"1\" which means Learning  \n    if (stateStr === '1.0' || stateStr === '1') {\n      return 'learning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"3.0\" or \"3\" which means Relearning\n    if (stateStr === '3.0' || stateStr === '3') {\n      return 'relearning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"0\" or \"0.0\" which means New\n    if (stateStr === '0' || stateStr === '0.0') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle string states\n    const validStates = ['new', 'learning', 'review', 'relearning'];\n    if (validStates.includes(stateStr.toLowerCase())) {\n      return stateStr.toLowerCase();\n    }\n    \n    // Default: if repetitions is 0, treat as new\n    if (!repetitions || repetitions === 0) {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Otherwise treat as review\n    return 'review';\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Set initial values with defaults\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    card.difficulty = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    \n    // Normalize state before mapping\n    const normalizedState = this.normalizeState(dbCard.state, dbCard.repetitions);\n    \n    // Map normalized state to FSRS State\n    switch (normalizedState) {\n      case 'new':\n        card.state = State.New;\n        card.due = now; // New cards are due immediately\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'learning':\n        card.state = State.Learning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'relearning':\n        card.state = State.Relearning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'review':\n      default:\n        card.state = State.Review;\n        // For review cards, set due date properly\n        if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n        } else {\n          card.due = now;\n        }\n        \n        // Calculate stability from interval for review cards\n        // FSRS stability roughly correlates to interval * ease_factor\n        // This is an approximation - the actual stability is learned through reviews\n        const interval = dbCard.interval || 0;\n        const easeFactor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n        card.stability = Math.max(0.1, interval * easeFactor); // Minimum stability of 0.1\n        \n        // Calculate elapsed_days from last_review or due_date\n        if (dbCard.last_review) {\n          card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.last_review) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          // If no last_review but has due_date, calculate from due_date\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.due) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else {\n          card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        }\n        break;\n    }\n    \n    // Set last_review if available\n    if (dbCard.last_review) {\n      card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n    } else {\n      card.last_review = now;\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: rating = Rating.Easy; break; // Perfect maps to Easy with bonus\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result - pass card first, then now\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days from now to the scheduled due date\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    const intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling.card.lapses,\n      state: stateMap[scheduling.card.state] || 'new',\n      stability: scheduling.card.stability,\n      difficulty: scheduling.card.difficulty\n    };\n  },\n  \n  // Calculate preview intervals without modifying card\n  previewIntervals(card, ratingValue) {\n    const fsrsCard = this.dbToCard(card);\n    return this.repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue);\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = FSRSEngine;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772160125083}}
{"type":"message","id":"8eb9656a","parentId":"ea0dcb8f","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:42:47.109Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to fix the issues:\n\n1. **Fix stability calculation**: The current calculation `interval * ease_factor` is wrong. For review cards, we should use the interval directly as a rough approximation of stability, or use a more appropriate formula. Looking at FSRS, stability is actually learned through reviews. For a simple approximation, we can use the interval directly (or interval * some factor).\n\n2. **Fix Rating 5 (Perfect)**: Currently maps to Rating.Easy. We need to apply a bonus. One way is to use Rating.Easy but then add a bonus to the interval. Or we can use a different approach.\n\nLet me fix both issues:","thinkingSignature":"f7f7b2703f8d4398185d7a9d99ac5be53e0bf1b28394802378972865d1d289e3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cordabpqwase_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Normalize state value to standard string\n  normalizeState(dbState, repetitions) {\n    // Handle undefined, null, or empty states\n    if (!dbState || dbState === '') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle numeric states (convert to string)\n    const stateStr = String(dbState).trim();\n    \n    // Handle \"2.0\" or \"2\" which means Review\n    if (stateStr === '2.0' || stateStr === '2') {\n      return 'review';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"1.0\" or \"1\" which means Learning  \n    if (stateStr === '1.0' || stateStr === '1') {\n      return 'learning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"3.0\" or \"3\" which means Relearning\n    if (stateStr === '3.0' || stateStr === '3') {\n      return 'relearning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"0\" or \"0.0\" which means New\n    if (stateStr === '0' || stateStr === '0.0') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle string states\n    const validStates = ['new', 'learning', 'review', 'relearning'];\n    if (validStates.includes(stateStr.toLowerCase())) {\n      return stateStr.toLowerCase();\n    }\n    \n    // Default: if repetitions is 0, treat as new\n    if (!repetitions || repetitions === 0) {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Otherwise treat as review\n    return 'review';\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Set initial values with defaults\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    card.difficulty = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    \n    // Normalize state before mapping\n    const normalizedState = this.normalizeState(dbCard.state, dbCard.repetitions);\n    \n    // Map normalized state to FSRS State\n    switch (normalizedState) {\n      case 'new':\n        card.state = State.New;\n        card.due = now; // New cards are due immediately\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'learning':\n        card.state = State.Learning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'relearning':\n        card.state = State.Relearning;\n        card.due = dbCard.due_date ? new Date(dbCard.due_date) : now;\n        card.stability = 0;\n        card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        break;\n      case 'review':\n      default:\n        card.state = State.Review;\n        // For review cards, set due date properly\n        if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n        } else {\n          card.due = now;\n        }\n        \n        // Use the interval directly as stability approximation\n        // This is more accurate than interval * ease_factor\n        // FSRS stability represents how stable the memory is\n        const interval = dbCard.interval || 0;\n        card.stability = Math.max(0.1, interval);\n        \n        // Calculate elapsed_days from last_review or due_date\n        if (dbCard.last_review) {\n          card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.last_review) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          // If no last_review but has due_date, calculate from due_date\n          card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - card.due) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n        } else {\n          card.elapsed_days = 0;\n        }\n        break;\n    }\n    \n    // Set last_review if available\n    if (dbCard.last_review) {\n      card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n    } else {\n      card.last_review = now;\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    let perfectBonus = 1.0; // Default no bonus\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: \n        rating = Rating.Easy; \n        perfectBonus = 1.3; // 30% bonus for Perfect\n        break;\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result - pass card first, then now\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days from now to the scheduled due date\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    let intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    let intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Apply Perfect bonus if applicable\n    if (perfectBonus > 1.0) {\n      intervalDays = intervalDays * perfectBonus;\n    }\n    \n    // For Again (rating 1), return a learning interval instead of 0\n    // FSRS uses relearning state, so we show a reasonable learning time\n    if (ratingValue === 1) {\n      // Show 10 minutes as learning interval\n      intervalDays = 10 / (24 * 60); // 10 minutes in days\n    }\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling.card.lapses,\n      state: stateMap[scheduling.card.state] || 'new',\n      stability: scheduling.card.stability,\n      difficulty: scheduling.card.difficulty\n    };\n  },\n  \n  // Calculate preview intervals without modifying card\n  previewIntervals(card, ratingValue) {\n    const fsrsCard = this.dbToCard(card);\n    return this.repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue);\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = FSRSEngine;\n","file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/src/fsrs.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":21299,"output":1871,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30959,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160125086}}
