{"type":"message","id":"c0beddee","parentId":"c81bd98e","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:45:10.705Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! The FSRS library does return different intervals for new cards:- Rating 1 (Again): ~1 minute- Rating 2 (Hard): ~4 minutes- Rating 3 (Good): ~10 minutes- Rating 4 (Easy): 6 days\n\nThe issue is that in my fix, I hardcoded the \"Again\" rating to always show 10 minutes. But the FSRS library actually calculates different intervals for each rating. Let me check why Rating 2 shows 0m - it's probably because of very small intervals that get rounded to 0.Let me fix the fsrs.js to properly handle all these cases instead of hardcoding:","thinkingSignature":"fe217451241b5b6709e8e5a1ef729413d4bee78d0b86c56648f4399d8c654c94"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2k6906qdy1fl_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst FSRSEngine = require('./src/fsrs');\n\nconst db = new Database('./data/cards.db');\nconst newCard = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT * FROM cards WHERE state = 'new' LIMIT 1\\\").get();\n\n// Test with the engine\nfor (let rating = 1; rating <= 5; rating++) {\n  const result = FSRSEngine.previewIntervals(newCard, rating);\n  console.log('Rating', rating, ':', result ? 'interval=' + result.interval + ' days' : 'null');\n}\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":35340,"output":300,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43429,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160303599}}
