{"type":"message","id":"2dd49571","parentId":"260fc22c","timestamp":"2026-02-27T02:47:37.058Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so this is working correctly! The issue must be in my FSRSEngine code. Let me look at the repeat function more closely - maybe I'm not passing the correct parameters to fsrs.repeat().\n\nWait - I think I see the issue now! Let me check the repeat function in fsrs.js:\n\n```javascript\nconst result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n```\n\nBut in my earlier debug, I'm calling `fsrs.repeat(fsrsCard, rating)` but that doesn't make sense. Let me check how I'm actually calling it:\n\nLooking at my code:\n```javascript\nconst result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\nconst scheduling = result[rating];\n```\n\nThis is correct. But wait - I'm passing `card` (the FSRS Card object), not `fsrsCard`. Let me double-check my code.\n\nActually, wait. The problem might be that I'm clearing the require cache but the old code is still cached. Let me restart Node completely and test:","thinkingSignature":"8b2e81b9a083c553431ce69ca766bb029ff48337a0476d96edeca53a102dd4c4"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9kzhyym6cmbb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node --version"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":45112,"output":240,"cacheRead":7789,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53141,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772160448187}}
